              "title": "Server-side request forgery supported by source analysis",
              "summary": "A request-derived value ($request-\u003eget('url')) controls the destination of file_get_contents with no enforced destination restriction (CWE-918). This is a static source judgment, not runtime network reachability, DNS, redirect or deployment-policy analysis, or independent Findings Review.",
              "input_validation": "Not established from the supplied evidence.",
              "use_protection": "SSRF assessment: destination control full_url, restriction none, coverage incomplete. Scanner policy: A consistent SSRF answer is supported by an independent request-to-destination path through a verified file_get_contents binding with no enforced destination restriction. Unresolved sibling paths remain visible. This is a static judgment, not runtime network reachability, DNS or redirect analysis, or independent Findings Review.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. Network policy, proxies, cloud metadata reachability and redirect targets are not inferred. Unresolved sibling paths, if any, remain separate blocking or coverage records.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Keep request data from choosing the outbound destination",
                "actions": [
                  "At src/Services/Avatar.php:18, stop passing $request-\u003eget('url') as the destination of file_get_contents unless it is first restricted to trusted destinations.",
                  "Prefer selecting the destination from a fixed table of trusted URLs by a request-supplied key instead of accepting a URL.",
                  "Otherwise parse the URL and require its scheme and host to match a finite allow-list before the request, rejecting on failure. A string prefix, substring or regular-expression test on the raw text is not a restriction.",
                  "Disable redirect following, or re-check each redirect target against the same allow-list, and decide whether internal address ranges must be blocked after DNS resolution."
                ],
